cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Double Torus — A Deterministic Quantum Simulation Kernel with Content-Addressed Verification"
abstract: >-
  The double-torus vortex algebra of the sequence 12487536901, with the Clay
  Millennium problems as proof of concept. Every claim recomputes from src/0. 731
  registered theorems, 725 of them carrying an executable proof. 20 Lean 4 proof
  files compile in plain Lean with no Mathlib and no `sorry`; 84 involution
  theorems and 29 registry rows are decided by the kernel with no axiom. This work
  does NOT prove, solve, or resolve any Clay Millennium Prize Problem: it proves
  the involution each problem is stated across, and an involution is not the
  conjecture. Earlier drafts asserted such proofs; they were withdrawn after the
  2026-08-20 audit (HONESTY.md).

authors:
  - family-names: Rouschev
    given-names: Tsvetan
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0000-7312-9778"
    affiliation: Independent Research

type: software
date-released: "2026-09-14"

identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: "10.5281/zenodo.22352566"
    description: >-
      CITE THIS FOR THE SOFTWARE. The concept DOI of the release archive: it
      resolves to the newest archived release and follows every future one
      (currently v1.5.0, record 22737368, linked isSupplementTo the v1.5.0 tag).
      A citation of this DOI reaches the software as released, which the
      priority record below does not.
  - type: doi
    value: "10.5281/zenodo.21787144"
    description: >-
      THE FIRST DEPOSIT — 2026-08-04, Tsvetan Rouschev — and the priority record
      kept as such: the earliest dated, authored statement of the ℤ/9 involution
      approach to the Clay Millennium problems, published before any later work
      on the same ground. It is retained precisely so the date and the authorship
      stand on the public record, independently recomputable from the deposit.
      Its title, "Quantum Proofs of the Clay Millennium Problems v1.0", carries
      claims the author's own 2026-08-20 audit withdrew — this repository asserts
      no Clay problem is solved by it; see the abstract above and HONESTY.md.
      Cited for PRIORITY and attribution, not as proof, and not for its title.
      NOTE its concept DOI (10.5281/zenodo.21787143) is shared with two unrelated
      works and now resolves to the uuidna record, so cite this VERSION DOI and
      never that concept.
